{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124240","id":4764843404,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHAG9jA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124240","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124240.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124240.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124240","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124240/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124240/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124240/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/617cbb803f08d65c1d095dd39b468fb6f7d51b5d","number":124240,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add missing AABB constructor with 6 `real_t` values","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is the same as PR #104113, but for AABB instead of Projection.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen GDExtension generates bindings, it creates C++ code based on the API JSON. Values are serialized into literals constructed with numbers matching the value, for example, `Vector3(0, 1, 0)`. This includes default values for function parameters. AABB default values are serialized like `AABB(0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1)`. However, Godot is missing a constructor for AABB, so the generated C++ code doesn't compile:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1328\" height=\"258\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-06 142244\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9fc9463a-26ad-4a41-8b07-8adbb999560e\" />\r\n\r\nI encountered this problem when the CI checks for godot-cpp failed to compile with my 4D module, because one of the bound methods includes an AABB default value, which cannot be constructed, as seen in the above image. This wasn't a problem in the engine before because the engine doesn't have any AABB default values in parameters.\r\n\r\nNote: I believe to fix the *exact* problem, it only needs to be added to godot-cpp (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/2063). However, we should make the same change in the engine for consistency.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nNo AI was used at all, except to check that there are no other Variant types that need a `real_t` constructor.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/go